This is a plain regular FILE, not a directory.

It exists only so that .github/workflows/arb-queue-fail-closed.yml can pass
its path as the `dir` input to `mbeacom/adrkit/packages/ci/queue@<pin>`.
adrkit's corpus loader calls Node's `readdir()` on whatever path is given for
`dir`; calling `readdir()` on a file (rather than a directory) throws
`ENOTDIR` synchronously, before adrkit's queue Action constructs a GitHub
client or makes any API call (see queue-action-entrypoint.ts in adrkit:
"Corpus load is the first boundary; if it throws, fail before touching
GitHub."). That makes this fixture a deterministic, real, invalid-input
trigger for the Action's fail-closed path with a mechanically provable
zero-write guarantee -- not a corpus-content/schema error, which adrkit
instead reports as findings inside an issue body it still writes.

The content of this file is never read by adrkit: only the path's existence
as a non-directory matters. Do not turn this into a directory or delete it
without updating .github/workflows/arb-queue-fail-closed.yml and
README.md accordingly.
